in this video i'm going to share with  you the 10 apps that changed my life  they took me from a broke uni student to  a thriving entrepreneur what's going on  guys my name is david thomich i'm a  registered architect here in western  australia and over the last five years  i've owned four companies started a  satellite office got married worked full  time successfully been promoted every  single year whilst getting eight hours  of sleep every single night now you may  ask apps today we're starting the  discussion with an app that will  literally brighten up your life and your  entire morning but if you pay close  attention throughout this entire video  i've hidden an easter egg somewhere  between this time stamp so drop a  comment down below if you manage to spot  it the first app on this list is the  philips hue app now traditionally the  philips 2 app can do many many things  and it requires you to go out and also  purchase some sort of philips products  but specifically for this video what i'm  talking about is the sunrise feature in  the philips hue home app basically what  it allows you to do is you have to  purchase a philips hue light globe and  the philips hue bridge to be able to  activate it with your wi-fi system  but it will allow you to mimic the  sunrise and when winter comes around our  productivity significantly drops so by  simply automating the lighting in your  bedroom to turn on at the same time as  your alarm is going to significantly  improve your productivity throughout  that day because you're more likely to  get up when your alarm goes off now once  we get to a certain point in our life  stress and anxiety are unavoidable  especially if we're trying to push the  barriers of what can be achieved in a  single day so that's why health and  fitness are so important and personally  i believe have allowed me to take  success to a whole new level and it is  for that reason that my fitness power  makes it on this list my fitness power  allows me to track all of my macros and  basically understand what i'm putting  into my body how much my body needs to  be able to function properly because  once you stop exercising once you stop  eating correctly and once you stop  sleeping you're unable to achieve  anything and none of these apps will be  able to help you in life so you have to  understand and control that element  before you can move on to the next  stages third on the list is an app that  could make you financially free in the  future but not essentially immediately  it is an app that requires a substantial  amount of investment from both time  money and education but it is something  that is going to change your life so the  app that i use for this is the comsec  app which is specific to australia there  are hundreds of them out there basically  it is just an app that allows you to  trade on the stock market personally i  like to trade for a dividend portfolio  to be able to provide dividends and a  passive stream of income throughout the  year that way i don't have to worry  about where the money is coming from it  will continuously just keep coming but  overall by investing into some sort of  financial portfolio either be stocks  bonds or even real estate you're  basically setting up your future self  for a much better life your future self  will only thank you if your present self  actually does the work though so to stay  organized and focused across a diverse  portfolio of companies and of course a  full-time job i use a number of apps to  stay productive and stay on task first  of all is microsoft to do this is one of  the simplest apps you can download it is  a very very basic to-do list but it will  allow you to keep track of everything  that's going on and not forget about it  one of the biggest challenges i was  finding for myself personally  was simply remembering everything that  was going on in my day so now i have a  variety of lists that all track  different things and whenever i remember  that i need to do something i can jump  on the to-do list add it to the list and  then come back to it when i have time by  getting into the habit of using this  to-do list for everything in your life  it is going to make it significantly  easier to use it in your professional  life and improve productivity  so simply adding things like your  shopping list and all your chores at  home as well or even just your weekend  to-do list you can easily then convert  that habit into your professional life  and increase your productivity speaking  of productivity notion is the next app  on my list and as an architect this is a  critical app for me to basically  remember where every single project is  up to at the moment i'm currently  managing anywhere from 40 to 50 projects  per year which means i have to remember  40 to 50 project timelines consultants  information and everything that goes  with it for me i use notion as an  everyday journal whenever a project is  updated ever so slightly i update the  journal so that even if that project  pauses for a few months i can come back  to that notion page review exactly what  i wrote down and know where that project  is at as long as you stay up to date  with your notion journaling then you're  always going to be able to reflect and  be more productive yes it may take more  time up front to be able to actually  input that data but when the workflow  and the work amount becomes so large  that you genuinely can't remember  everything this 10 minutes spent on  updating a journal is gonna save you  hours in the long run the next app on  this list i guarantee every one of you  will have some version of it for me  personally it is onedrive onedrive is an  essential app to be able to do your work  anywhere remotely now in a world that is  ever changing and our work environment  is ever changing onedrive allows us  basically to work from home work from  the office or work anywhere remotely  without having to carry flash drive cd  drives or anything that we had to do  previously all we have to do is make  sure that everything is saved to the  onedrive before turning off our computer  and the rest you don't have to worry  about so simply by mitigating one extra  thing that you have to remember allows  your brain to remember one other thing  and when it comes to documents folders  and projects it means that you don't  have to go back to the office pick  something up come home redo that work  and then continue with your day you  could be potentially saving yourself  hours every single time this occurs  by simply using a cloud-based storage  system now this app is specific to  architecture and it has changed my  workflow entirely morfolio trace has  made my life so simple and all i really  have to do is carry around one ipad  rather than your typical architect  walking around with hundreds of rolls of  paper  a briefcase a pencil case rulers and all  the works portfolio trace is basically  butter paper on an ipad it allows you to  link to onedrive download all of your  files directly into the trace app sketch  over anything that you need and generate  ideas very very quickly so as an  architect more folio trace has been  pivotal in my workflow and it has been  used every single day for the last i  don't even know four or five years since  i've owned and used the app the next app  on this list actually changed my life  for the worse it didn't change it for  the better however there is a way that  you can change it for the better without  actually having to terminate that app  completely so the app i'm talking about  is outlook and outlook obviously is just  a simple mail client that continuously  just sends us notification after  notification after notification and it  gets rather draining so when you have  outlook connected to your phone and have  all of your emails constantly hitting  and vibrating it really starts to stress  you out after a while so what i've  discovered to work extremely well is  focus modes on the iphone basically what  i've implemented is a focus mode for  personal and work mode so whenever i  want to have some personal time to  actually work on things that i need to  achieve be going to the gym being eating  healthy meal prepping or doing anything  in between even something as simple as  just relaxing i have personal mode  turned on so none of those distractions  come through and it actually allows me  to be present in that moment rather than  focusing on what the distractions are  coming up on the phone whereas when i  need to be productive and i need to  actually achieve something for work then  i turn it on to work mode and it allows  all those notifications to come through  so it is a very simple feature set up on  your phone and i highly recommend  everybody does this if you're getting  constant distractions and notifications  the second last app on this list has  been around for decades and most likely  you've heard of it you've used it and  you know exactly what it is microsoft  excel is the app that has changed my  life in more ways than one but  understanding how to create good excel  spreadsheets i've been able to manage  everything in my life so much easier but  at the same time i've also been able to  do my job as an architect significantly  better so in a personal life you have  all of your finances and your budgeting  to track which can be done very quickly  and very easily through an excel  document by understanding your personal  finances it puts you in a significantly  better place every single year and makes  you actively think about what you're  spending your money on and how you're  spending the money whereas as an  architect understanding excel is pivotal  every so often we have to administer  contracts which means we have to review  progress claims and understand large  sums of money it becomes incredibly  confusing and incredibly difficult to  review hundreds and hundreds of invoices  without having some sort of system in  place to actually track everything  that's going on and break down all of  these claims now excel isn't the be-all  end-all there are multiple versions and  alternatives out there but excel is such  a simple program to use and there are so  many guides out there that you can learn  it relatively quickly to help you change  your life the last app on this list is  one that is going to change your life  but also free up your time i've been  using fiverr recently to be able to  produce high quality 3d architectural  renders to save myself significant time  by simply finding a good threaded  renderer online handing over the project  to them within a matter of days or a  matter of hours you can have high  quality work completed to your standards  for significantly less time and  investment than you would ever think so  more to point here delegating work  through online communities and online  apps such as fiverr will allow you to  free up your time that way you can again  increase your productivity in that 16  hours of critical time allowed in a day  anyway that's all for me today guys  thank you so much for watching if you  enjoyed the video make sure you check  out the playlist to the side of me for  more great architectural content if you  love the video make sure you smash that  subscribe button down below but like  always i'll see you next monday

